    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3219": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Mathematics",
      "description": "Department: UM Mathematics JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Orono, ME, United States The University of Maine is a community of more than 11,900 undergraduate and graduate students, and 2,500 employees located on the Orono campus, the regional campus in Machias, and throughout the state. UMaine is a land, sea and space grant university, and maintains a leadership role as the University of Maine System's flagship institution. UMaine is the state's public research university and a Carnegie R1 top-tier research institution, dedicated to providing excellent teaching, research and service for Maine, the nation and the world. The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at the University of Maine invites applications for an ongoing teaching position at the rank of Lecturer, with an anticipated start date of August 31, 2027. During the 9-month academic year, lecturers normally teach three classes per semester. This 10.5 month position also includes 1.5 months of summer mathematics instruction (June 1 – July 15) during which 2 classes will be taught, likely online. The salary range for this 10.5 month position is $66,000 - $75,000, commensurate with qualifications and experience. This position is ongoing, contingent upon satisfactory performance. Lecturers at the University of Maine have a promotion track and \"just cause\" protection after 6 years of service. Essential duties and responsibilities include but are not limited to: a mixture of both in-person and online undergraduate teaching in mathematics and/or statistics at the 100-level, course coordination, assessment, curriculum development, and/or other leadership activity related to instruction. Additional summer teaching opportunities may be available with additional compensation. Service to the department and university, participating collegially in the life of the department, and engaging in activities that enhance one’s professional development are also expected. This is an in-person, on-campus position. About the University: The University of Maine is a community of more than 11,900 undergraduate and graduate students, and 2,500 employees located on the Orono campus, the regional campus in Machias, and throughout the state. UMaine is a land, sea and space grant university, and maintains a leadership role as the University of Maine System's flagship institution. UMaine is the state's public research university and a Carnegie R1 top-tier research institution, dedicated to providing excellent teaching, research and service for Maine, the nation and the world. More information about UMaine is at umaine.edu . The University of Maine offers a wide range of benefits for employees including, but not limited to, tuition benefits (employee and dependent), comprehensive insurance coverage including medical, dental, vision, life insurance, and short and long term disability as well as retirement plan options. UMaine is located in beautiful Central Maine. Many employees report that a primary reason for choosing to come to UMaine is quality of life. Numerous cultural activities, excellent public schools, safe neighborhoods, high quality medical care, little traffic, and a reasonable cost of living make the greater Bangor area a wonderful place to live. Visit the Maine Office of Tourism to learn more about what the Bangor region has to offer. Qualifications: Required: A bachelor’s degree or higher in mathematics, applied mathematics, or statistics. A graduate degree (master’s or higher) in mathematics, applied mathematics, statistics, or mathematics education. Evidence of excellent teaching of college-level mathematics. Effective written and oral communication skills. Preferred: Breadth of teaching experience will be given some preference, depending on the relevance of the classes taught to the needs of the department. Evidence of involvement in curriculum development, assessment, or similar professional activities relevant to the position. Other Information: To be considered for this position you will need to “Apply” and upload the documentation listed below: A cover letter describing your relevant background and how you meet the job requirements and qualifications as described above, A curriculum vitae that includes your relevant qualifications and experiences, Copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts (unofficial is fine for now, though official copies may be requested at time of hire), A teaching portfolio consisting of a teaching statement, recent syllabi from classes taught, and copies of student teaching evaluations (both numerical and qualitative) from the four most recent terms taught. The above materials must also be submitted through Mathjobs . In addition: At least three letters of reference, at least two of which address your teaching, are required in Mathjobs , but NOT here in Oracle Recruiting. Applications received by 11:59pm EST on November 5, 2026 will receive full consideration. Review of applications will begin on November 6, 2026. Late applications may be considered at the discretion of the committee. Incomplete applications cannot be considered. Applicants who are not US citizens or current green-card holders must currently reside in the United States and possess a valid immigration status that allows the University to petition for an H-1B transfer or change of status. We are unable to provide sponsorship for individuals who reside outside the U.S. and would require a new visa to enter the country for this position. The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screening. The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you wish to have a paper copy of the ASR or you need to have a copy of the ASR in an accessible format, the University will provide such a copy upon request. Please contact: UMaine Police Department, 81 Rangeley Rd., The University of Maine, Orono, ME 04469-5794, or call 207.581.4053. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3234": {
      "title": "PFAS Data Manager",
      "description": "Department: UM Administration NFA JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Orono, ME, United States The University of Maine is a community of more than 11,900 undergraduate and graduate students, and 2,500 employees located on the Orono campus, the regional campus in Machias, and throughout the state. UMaine is a land, sea and space grant university, and maintains a leadership role as the University of Maine System's flagship institution. UMaine is the state's public research university and a Carnegie R1 top-tier research institution, dedicated to providing excellent teaching, research and service for Maine, the nation and the world. The PFAS Data Manager will oversee the analysis and curation of per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) research data as part of a long-term Center of Excellence created through a partnership with the USDA Agricultural Research Service. This position will perform two primary functions. First, it will consult with researchers across the project to support their data analysis needs, including data structure, workflows, and long-term preservation. Second, the Data Manager will establish, share, and maintain guidance for data curation created through the Center of Excellence. Typical hiring range for this soft-money funded position is $70,000 to $80,000 commensurate with qualifications and experience. Please review the PFAS Data Manager job description for more information. About the University: The University of Maine is a community of more than 11,900 undergraduate and graduate students, and 2,500 employees located on the Orono campus, the regional campus in Machias, and throughout the state. UMaine is a land, sea and space grant university, and maintains a leadership role as the University of Maine System's flagship institution. UMaine is the state's public research university and a Carnegie R1 top-tier research institution, dedicated to providing excellent teaching, research and service for Maine, the nation and the world. More information about UMaine is at umaine.edu . The University of Maine offers a wide range of benefits for employees including, but not limited to, tuition benefits (employee and dependent), comprehensive insurance coverage including medical, dental, vision, life insurance, and short and long term disability as well as retirement plan options. UMaine is located in beautiful Central Maine. Many employees report that a primary reason for choosing to come to UMaine is quality of life. Numerous cultural activities, excellent public schools, safe neighborhoods, high quality medical care, little traffic, and a reasonable cost of living make the greater Bangor area a wonderful place to live. Visit the Maine Office of Tourism to learn more about what the Bangor region has to offer. Qualifications: Required: A master’s degree in data science or closely related discipline or an equivalent combination of education and experience, and 3 or more years of experience in research data management or a similar position Proficiency in one or more programming and data analysis languages commonly used for scientific data manipulation Demonstrated experience managing, integrating, validating, and analyzing complex scientific or research datasets in a high-performance and/or cloud computing setting Excellent analytical, troubleshooting and problem-solving skills, in particular with respect to data quality and integration issues Strong written and verbal communication skills, with demonstrated ability to communicate technical concepts to researchers and other audiences with varying levels of technical expertise Preferred: Ph.D. in data science or a field topically related to PFAS Experience supporting data management within a higher education, research center, laboratory, or other collaborative research environment Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across multidisciplinary teams and with diverse stakeholders of researchers, students, technical staff and administrators and to manage competing priorities and data needs Familiarity with data types associated with PFAS research, including environmental sampling, analytical chemistry, toxicology, remediation and EPA PFAS analytical methods and associated data reporting requirements Familiarity with FAIR data principles (Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, and Reusable), research data repositories, and data-sharing requirements associated with federally funded research Other Information: To be considered for this position you will need to “Apply” and upload the documentation listed below: 1.) a cover letter which describes your experience, interests, and suitability for the position 2.) a resume/curriculum vitae Candidates selected to proceed to the final stages of the search process will be requested to provide a list of names and contact information for references. Incomplete application materials cannot be considered. Materials received after the initial review date will be reviewed at the discretion of the University. For full consideration, materials must be submitted by 4:30 p.m. EST on November 2, 2026. The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screening. The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you wish to have a paper copy of the ASR or you need to have a copy of the ASR in an accessible format, the University will provide such a copy upon request. Please contact: UMaine Police Department, 81 Rangeley Rd., The University of Maine, Orono, ME 04469-5794, or call 207.581.4053. "
