    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3034": {
      "title": "Organic Chemistry Laboratory Manager and Teaching Associate",
      "description": "Department: UM Chemistry JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Orono, ME, United States The University of Maine is a community of more than 11,900 undergraduate and graduate students, and 2,500 employees located on the Orono campus, the regional campus in Machias, and throughout the state. UMaine is a land, sea and space grant university, and maintains a leadership role as the University of Maine System's flagship institution. UMaine is the state's public research university and a Carnegie R1 top-tier research institution, dedicated to providing excellent teaching, research and service for Maine, the nation and the world. The primary purpose of this position is to prepare supplies and materials for organic chemistry laboratories, maintain the organic chemistry prep room, including chemical inventories and waste management, and to teach up to two organic lab sections during the fall and spring and up to one in each of the two summer sessions. The hiring range for this position is $50,000 to $53,000 commensurate with qualifications and experience. Please review the Organic Chemistry Laboratory Manager and Teaching Associate job description for more information. About the University: The University of Maine is a community of more than 11,900 undergraduate and graduate students, and 2,500 employees located on the Orono campus, the regional campus in Machias, and throughout the state. UMaine is a land, sea and space grant university, and maintains a leadership role as the University of Maine System's flagship institution. UMaine is the state's public research university and a Carnegie R1 top-tier research institution, dedicated to providing excellent teaching, research and service for Maine, the nation and the world. More information about UMaine is at umaine.edu . The University of Maine offers a wide range of benefits for employees including, but not limited to, tuition benefits (employee and dependent), comprehensive insurance coverage includin